Thanks for your comments, xorxes. I agree that "invite" is not exactly the 
same meaning as "curmi", but I think "curmi" will do in this context.

Also, you make a good point that I had the place structure of "curmi" wrong, 
although I have no idea why "curmi" is designed this way, without a place in 
its structure for the agent who is being allowed to do something. It makes 
the saying of something like this quite awkward.

Your suggestion of "pagbu lo nu cuxna" seems to make cmicu'a unnecessary, 
but I think we should probably have a more specific way of talking about an 
election in cases where it needs to be distinguished from other forms of 
mass choosing. Perhaps I should simply use "cuxnrvoto".

mi'e .sen.


